00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:08,017
If I smash it into the
pavement from this high?

249
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:10,982
That should be enough to
shatter its ass to bits!

250
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:14,140
I don't think so.

251
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:18,460
Oh no! Mista!

252
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,320
Holy shit.

253
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:34,400
He was telling the truth after all.

254
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,980
Everything went just as he said.

255
00:14:38,940 --> 00:14:42,587
As long as you don't see your
own mug carved inside the stone,

256
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:46,380
you get to live on for at
least another day. Nice.

257
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:49,787
What the hell were you
doing in there, Mista?

258
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:55,229
You left the recorder in the
car after your tantrum, doofus.

259
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:56,590
Oh, hey.

260
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:58,180
It's you, Fugo.

261
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:07,940
So what on earth were you in the end?

262
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:12,472
Mista, I'd very much like the
explanation you promised me.

263
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,339
I mean, none of it matters anymore.

264
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:16,850
I...

265
00:15:16,933 --> 00:15:19,760
I wouldn't know where to
begin, even. Oh, wait.

266
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,841
How about the old man's daughter?

267
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:24,120
It's the boyfriend, I'd say.

268
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:28,140
But technically, it also wasn't him.

269
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:34,840
Either way, he's not leaving the
hospital for at least a few months, so...

270
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:37,440
Unhelpfully vague as ever. Classic.

271
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:39,720
Is he a friend?

272
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,220
Or do we kick his ass?

273
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:43,080
Also, was it suicide?

274
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,774
Why don't you start from the beginning?

275
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,637
But see, that's the thing, though.

276
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,240
It's really hard to, you know,

277
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:53,697
piece this whole thing together
in a way that makes sense.

278
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:54,610
Look,

279
00:15:54,693 --> 00:15:57,357
all you need to know is that I
destroyed the mean old rock stand,

280
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,060
so everything's peachy now.

281
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:07,017
Oh yeah, how's about you let me take
over the whole leaky eye Luca thing?

282
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:07,930
No thanks.

283
00:16:08,013 --> 00:16:09,626
I've decided to do it myself.

284
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,937
Your reporting skills would slow things.

285
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:14,255
I believe I'll do just fine on my own.

286
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:18,500
Fugo, our florist friend
should get a detailed account.

287
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,660
Gather what you can from Mista.

288
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:24,460
Bucciarati, you know you
have my utmost respect.

289
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:28,160
But this guy here, he's a
puzzle even I can't solve.

290
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,137
Okay, don't hurt yourself.

291
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:36,220
We'll just have to use Abakio's...

292
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:40,160
So naive, do you really
believe this is the end?

293
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:45,720
If only you had accepted the stone's
mercy, all would be peaceful.

294
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:49,960
But you chose to remain enslaved to fate.

295
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:53,940
That which is carved in
stone cannot be changed.

296
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,380
Whoever you are, I hope you're ready.

297
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:00,240
A perilous journey of hardship awaits.

298
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:03,980
And for some of you, it
will be the last one.

299
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:08,440
I wonder, are all of you like him?

300
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:13,042
That young man flung
himself off a tall building,

301
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,500
all for a chance to save his friend.

302
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:21,700
Perhaps the path you are bound to walk
isn't one of meaningless suffering.

303
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:26,520
The adversity you'll endure may well
be the crucible of hope for another,

304
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:30,660
and perhaps it could be the
birth of a greater purpose.

305
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:35,032
Wishing for their safety will do nothing.

306
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:38,180
I can only hope that
they are sleeping slaves.

307
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:39,750
That's it.

308
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:45,720
Sleeping slaves will eventually awaken to
discover some meaning in their suffering.

309
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:54,917
Hey, what's the holdup?

310
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,717
Do you want me to heal Bucciarati?

311
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:57,630
Sure!

312
00:17:57,713 --> 00:17:59,891
Why don't I just rub my gun on his wounds?

313
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,572
Dude, are you listening?

314
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:04,880
Whoa there.

315
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:06,117
You gotta watch your step.

316
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,030
Thanks, Mista.

317
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:09,535
Something really weird just popped up.

318
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:21,410
Trish?

319
00:18:21,493 --> 00:18:22,520
Hey, Trish!

320
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:25,880
Where'd you go? Trish!

321
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:27,260
Hey, Giorno!

322
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:29,302
Where the hell did that girl go?

323
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:30,617
You startled me.

324
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:32,920
She's right there behind you. Look.

325
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,900
Guys, it's all right. I'm here.

326
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,917
The thing I tripped on
was next to the rock.

327
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:40,830
Check it out.

328
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:43,177
Don't go leaving me behind now.

329
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:45,025
Sorry I gave you all a fright.

330
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:47,197
I hope you'll still take me with you.

331
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:49,280
It's a long way for a lone turtle.

332
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:51,017
Why are you still here?

333
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:51,930
It's Mr.

334
00:18:52,013 --> 00:18:52,843
Polnareff.

335
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:56,277
How are you alive?

336
00:18:56,360 --> 00:19:00,157
If our souls were switched back to normal,
doesn't that mean yours should be...

337
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:01,897
Wait a minute, that's not right.

338
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:03,097
Wouldn't you...

339
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:04,300
and that?

340
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,660
My original body has perished.

341
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:09,509
But the moment my spirit
departed my flesh,

342
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:12,877
I made sure to hang on as tight
as I could to this turtle.

343
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:15,372
I'll remain bound to this key for a time.

344
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:18,971
I hope you won't mind little
old spectral me tagging along.

345
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:23,497
Hot damn, I'll admit I'm glad to
see you still kicking and stuff.

346
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,137
But the day's not over yet.

347
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:28,097
We still need to patch
out Bucciarati's injuries.

348
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:29,297
Wait, Bucciarati?

349
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:31,380
But I thought his soul was...

350
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:43,871
Whoa, what are you doing?

351
00:19:44,020 --> 00:19:45,320
Oh crap, my bad.

352
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:48,377
I was just thinking maybe
you might have had a point.

353
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,872
My pits, they actually do smell like ass.

354
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:54,017
Can't believe I'm just
now learning about this.

355
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:56,117
Maybe I should put on cologne after all.

356
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,030
What?

357
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:57,943
What?

358
00:19:58,420 --> 00:20:01,377
Look, I might have exaggerated
a little bit earlier.

359
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,937
Everything happens so fast.

360
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:04,857
Right now, I don't think
you smell that bad.

361
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:08,352
In a super weird kind of way,
it actually feels nostalgic.

362
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:11,560
Oh my gosh, do you really mean that?

363
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:14,398
Yeah, but your fingers are freakish.

364
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:23,240
So then, what's your choice?

365
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:28,033
When those who've left us
place their wills in our hands,

366
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:30,800
it is our sacred duty to carry it forth.

367
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,197
It remains.

368
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,420
That's my choice.

369
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:40,249
Why don't you keep the
arrow in the turtle?

370
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:43,120
That'll do, Giorno.

371
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:48,620
A worthy decision to fulfill
your duty as a survivor.

372
00:20:57,080 --> 00:21:01,340
Let us go to the Coliseum.

373
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:26,349
We have the mission,
they are the blessing,

374
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:30,520
but they dare to tell us
what's bad and what's good.

375
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:37,800
Stand up, join us, run,

376
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:39,620
I'll say this a lie,

377
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:45,060
we are the power, close to the
future, cause we are the fighters,

378
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:48,080
just fighting for a right.

379
00:23:03,060 --> 00:23:03,890
Thank you.
